body:
On the opposite, it's going to make things easier: you'll no longer pass `this.props.children` by mistake and expect it to work. To clarify, when you received named `children` in router, you're not supposed to just put them into `render`: you should do something like

``` js
render() {
  return (
    <div>
      {this.props.children.sidebar}
      {this.props.children.content}
    </div>
  )
}
```

It was never the intention for them to be used as `this.props.children` as an object map, so it's actually good that 0.14 doesn't support this anymore.
